WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.447
Forty-seven thousand Canadians dead from opioid toxicity since 2016.

00:00:05.397 --> 00:00:10.772
In 2023 alone: thirteen thousand, seven hundred and forty-one deaths.

00:00:10.772 --> 00:00:17.579
Fentanyl emergence in 2014 accelerated the death rate by over eight hundred percent in the hardest-hit regions.

00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:23.306
British Columbia: over seventeen hundred deaths per year — the highest per capita in Canada.

00:00:23.306 --> 00:00:30.715
Pharmaceutical companies manufactured and advertised opioids for minor pain conditions throughout the 1990s and 2000s.

00:00:30.715 --> 00:00:35.681
Criminal charges were filed against Purdue Pharma in 2020 for misleading marketing.

00:00:35.681 --> 00:00:41.443
Canada's opioid crisis began after American litigation forced recognition of the addiction risk.

00:00:41.443 --> 00:00:43.238
The same drugs.

00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:45.136
The same companies.

00:00:45.136 --> 00:00:46.897
The same denial.

00:00:46.897 --> 00:00:52.034
The only difference: forty-seven thousand Canadian families who will never get an answer.
